keywords:
  - hydraulic transmission
  - bubble compliance
  - air spring
  - variable stiffness
  - soft robotics
  - time constant
abstract: >-
  An experimental study of how trapped air bubbles change the static stiffness,
  dynamic response, and variable-stiffness capability of a small syringe
  hydraulic transmission. The report covers 1, 2, and 5 mL air volumes, measured
  static stiffness, step-response time constants, and a soft-joint demonstration,
  and provides the measured CSV data and analysis code.
